<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Locke returns two weeks after his sick visit for a cold that triggered a yellow-zone flare. He took up to 11 inhalations of budesonide-formoterol on the worst day and never needed prednisolone. His peak flow climbed back above 400 L/min by the fifth day and has been 420 to 440 since. The cold cleared in about a week, and he stopped acetaminophen after four days. The review planned for one week after the sick visit did not take place: the clinic&apos;s first slot was today. He now needs his reliever about once a week, sleeps through the night, and has no side effects from tiotropium (no dry mouth, difficulty passing urine, or eye pain). The open fires remain out of use. He would like his first zoster vaccine today. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Flare</td><td>Yellow zone with a cold; managed by the action plan without prednisolone</td></tr><tr><td>Peak flow</td><td>Back to 420 to 440 L/min; 430 in clinic today</td></tr><tr><td>Reliever use</td><td>About once a week</td></tr><tr><td>Tiotropium</td><td>Four months; no side effects</td></tr><tr><td>Asthma Control Test</td><td>21</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

